WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.440 --> 00:00:04.730
There are a few rules to follow when traversing
through the Marvel Cinematic Universe.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.940
The most important rule is one that's already
been long-established in comic books: death

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:13.530
isn't necessarily final, and some goodbyes
are really just "see you later"s.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:14.929
"So dead brother huh?"

00:00:14.929 --> 00:00:16.960
"Yeah, that could be annoying."

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.470
"Well, he's been dead before."

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:25.010
As it turns out, that last rule will apply
to the fourth Avengers movie in a big way.

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:29.130
It's not really a surprise that some dearly-departed
heroes are making their way back to life in

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.130
the super-sequel.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:34.950
But according to one MCU actor, the Infinity
War follow-up will be bringing one villain

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:37.390
back from the dead in a super clever way.

00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:42.249
And if he's telling the truth, the details
just might confirm a major fan theory.

00:00:42.249 --> 00:00:47.120
Speaking on the UFC Unfiltered podcast, actor
Frank Grillo revealed that Marvel fans can

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:52.670
expect to see him reprise his role as the
Hydra-agent-slash-terrorist Brock Rumlow,

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.690
also known as the comic book villain Crossbones.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:01:00.179
Now, you might be thinking, "Didn't Crossbones
pretty clearly die by blowing himself up at

00:01:00.179 --> 00:01:02.160
the start of Captain America: Civil War?"

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:03.999
Well, yes, he did.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:08.470
It was kind of a big deal, with his explosive
demise and the collateral damage it caused

00:01:08.470 --> 00:01:12.960
setting up the Sokovia Accords that still
affect the movies' universe to this day.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.260
Yeah, there's not really any coming back from
that one.

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:28.540
But it's not like the villain is returning
from the grave - instead, audiences will be

00:01:28.540 --> 00:01:31.290
going back to the time before he died.

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:35.920
It turns out, Grillo's Crossbones will actually
pop up in what he described as a flashback

00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:36.920
sequence.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.990
One might initially think that Grillo's remarks
were just to keep the rumor mill churning,

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:45.360
like other Avengers actors have done in the
past, but that doesn't seem to be the case.

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:49.520
Grillo made a point to mention that he can
spill as many details as he'd like since he's

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.600
not tied to a Marvel contract, and doesn't
expect to work with them again.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.730
It sounds fair to us, though we kind of doubt
that Marvel producers are all that happy about

00:01:57.730 --> 00:01:59.870
his decision to spill the beans.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:02.000
The actor's exact words were,

00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:06.370
"I'm allowed to say whatever I want because
I'm never doing another Marvel movie,"

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.750
But it's not because he doesn't like the company,
or the franchise.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:11.470
Apparently, he's just tired of the work it
takes to be a supervillain.

00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:16.210
Or, as he sarcastically put it, quote, "I'm
117 years old."

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:21.190
At one point in the period between Civil War
and Infinity War, Grillo sounded certain that

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:25.630
he was done playing Crossbones for good, and
even implied that he had turned down an opportunity

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:27.281
to return to the series.

00:02:27.281 --> 00:02:31.350
He shared those thoughts during a January
2017 interview with Collider, discussing his

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.200
departures from both The Purge franchise and
the MCU.

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.900
In the interview, he said,

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:39.750
"There's nowhere for it to go, unless you're
Captain America or Iron Man.

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.530
They were talking about it, but I was like,
'You know what?

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:44.120
I'd just rather not do it.'"

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:47.930
But apparently, something happened behind
the scenes to change the actor's mind.

00:02:47.930 --> 00:02:52.580
By September 2017, the actor was hinting at
a return appearance to the series.

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:54.360
During an interview with Forbes, he said,

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:58.880
"There is some [Marvel] news that nobody knows
yet, to do with my character, that's going

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:01.850
to be really interesting and I'm excited about
that."

00:03:01.850 --> 00:03:05.980
Almost a year later, in July 2018, Grillo
sparked even more rumors that he'd play a

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.780
part in Avengers 4 when he took to Instagram
and shared a collage photo of a Crossbones

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:12.640
action figure with the caption,

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.640
"Uhhhhh…… ok.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.430
I guess my life is complete."

00:03:15.430 --> 00:03:20.340
Of course, the first two hashtags in his post
referenced Grillo's appearances in the second

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:24.150
and third Captain America movies, but that
half-done third hashtag?

00:03:24.150 --> 00:03:27.610
Yeah, that's almost certainly a nod to Avengers
4.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:32.040
On the surface, Grillo's comments simply confirm
what seems like a very small plot point of

00:03:32.040 --> 00:03:35.580
Avengers 4: Crossbones will reappear in a
flashback scene.

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:40.080
But looking at the bigger picture, his remarks
actually seem to validate the longstanding

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:44.610
fan theory that the sequel will see the surviving
heroes from Infinity War travelling back in

00:03:44.610 --> 00:03:46.319
time to defeat Thanos.

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:50.400
The theory goes that they'll be using the
unique attributes of the Quantum Realm to

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:55.420
go back into the past and obtain the Infinity
Stones for themselves, effectively reversing

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:59.629
the events of Infinity War before the battle
with Thanos even begins.

00:03:59.629 --> 00:04:04.270
This theory first cropped up after fans got
a peek at Avengers 4 set photos that showed

00:04:04.270 --> 00:04:08.690
Chris Evans wearing his Captain America costume
from the Battle of New York sequence from

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:12.630
2012's Avengers, and it's been lingering in
fans' minds ever since.

00:04:12.630 --> 00:04:17.989
In that sense, Crossbones' reappearance will
be less of a flashback, and more of a do-over.

00:04:17.989 --> 00:04:22.060
As with everything out of the super-secretive
Marvel Studios, nothing is a guarantee until

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:27.090
the company comes right out and says it is
- and even then, it's still suspicious.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:31.020
The only way to know for sure what happens
is to be there when Avengers 4 takes off on

00:04:31.020 --> 00:04:32.690
May 3rd, 2019.

